<VI _name="lvai_af_add_hook.vi" description="Places ONE hook subVI on the top-level diagram of an override (or any class member) and wires it\2C in the ACTIVE PROJECT's application instance\3A an edit made in any other instance reports success and changes nothing. It does NOT save\3A the caller saves in a separate run\2C the way the measured kit routes do. Three kinds of wire\2C all found by NAME\3A\0A- SERIES (Series Panel Names[i]\2C Series Hook Near[i]\2C Series Hook Far[i])\3A the wire leaving that panel terminal is read\2C its far end remembered\2C the wire deleted\2C then panel terminal -&gt; hook Near terminal and hook Far terminal -&gt; the old far end. Before Call Parent that is panel `&lt;C&gt; in` with Near `&lt;C&gt; in`\2C Far `&lt;C&gt; out`\3B after Call Parent the panel is the indicator and the roles swap. The kit's pa_insert_series2 wiring\2C measured on Actor Core and Pre Launch Init.\0A- BRANCH (Branch Panel Names[i]\2C Branch Hook Names[i])\3A the panel terminal is tapped\2C nothing cut. The kit's af_add_hook_call wiring\2C measured.\0A- NODE (Source SubVI Name\2C Source Names[i]\2C Hook Names[i])\3A the top-level subVI node whose VI Name equals Source SubVI Name is the source\2C wired by lvbd_connect_by_names\2C which never picks an input that already carries a wire.\0AA name that matches nothing is listed under Missing and never guessed. A series insert assumes the panel's wire is ONE plain wire\3A the caller checks that first with lvai_af_hook_read. Requires lvbd_connect_by_names.vi to be open when this VI is generated. UNMEASURED as a whole.">
